# Architecture Boundaries LLM Guide

## Purpose

Validate code against configured dependency, layer-flow, and cycle rules.

## When To Run

- Before changing cross-module imports.
- After moving code between layers.
- Before finishing refactors that affect dependency direction.

## How To Read The Result

- Passing output means no configured boundary violation was found.
- Edge, flow, and cycle findings are blockers.
- Fix the owner or seam that makes the dependency point the wrong way.

## Examples

- Move persistence access behind the owning application seam.
- Replace private cross-module imports with the public seam.
- Break cycles by moving shared policy to the true owner.

## Agent Tips

- Treat findings as blockers.
- Do not add bypass imports.
- Rerun after import or ownership fixes.
